  "title": "pcapng module: Don't use a C++ reserved keyword for an identifier name",
  "description": "pcap_module.h is a public header with #ifdef __cplusplus, so it should\nsupport C++ compilation and not use C++ reserved keywords like \"new\" for\nidentifier names. Prevent compilation errors like:\n\ndebian/libwiretap-dev/usr/include/wireshark/wiretap/pcapng_module.h:321:13: error: expected unqualified-id before ‘new’\ndebian/libwiretap-dev/usr/include/wireshark/wiretap/pcapng_module.h:321:13: error: expected ‘)’ before ‘new’\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
